        "title": "perf(repair): stage validation proof gates",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- plan repair validation as ordered, risk-aware proof stages and independently rebuild exact proof semantics before replay\n- keep untrusted execution credential-free and lifecycle-script-free; bind immutable source, base, head, action, and output identities\n- publish only exact independently validated commit and tree bytes through credential-scoped mutation jobs\n- recheck live pause and structured security signals at every mutation boundary\n- checkpoint replacement publication before irreversible source closeout and recover only the exact authorized replacement PR\n- make retryable post-flight outcomes visible and durable for self-heal\n- resolve rerun handoff artifacts by trusted producer artifact ID and digest instead of consumer attempt names\n- reject unsafe command aliases and options, source mutation, proof drift, and terminal runtime budgets\n\n## Validation\n\n- Node 26.5.0 / pnpm 11.10.0\n- focused final-review regressions: 19 + 36 + 43 tests passed\n- full unit suite: 922/922 passed\n- full repair suite: 825/825 passed\n- changed coverage: 100% lines, 86.90% branches, 100% functions\n- aggregate coverage: 73.06% lines, 72.15% branches, 83.21% functions\n- full `pnpm run check` passed, including lint, builds, coverage, and format check\n- `pnpm run format` passed\n",
